Jahshaka patch 0077 — the light injection stores RADIANCE, and the specular cone's
eye-tuned 1/pi retires with the error it was cancelling.

MEDIA-only patch (`Samples/Media/VCT/LightInjection_piece_cs.any` and
`Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/Vct_piece_ps.any`). THE PROCESS COST IS STATED RATHER
THAN AVOIDED: Studio stages its media from the SOURCE tree
(cmake/IncludeOgre.cmake), so every tree must reset its ogre-next submodule and
re-run `irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` — no engine recompile beyond the staging,
but the loop must run. It OVERLAPS patches 0021, 0033, 0045, 0048, 0066, 0070 and
0074 in the pixel piece and 0076 in the injection piece, so a tree that already
carries those hits `build-ogre.sh`'s "Upstream changed the patched file" on a
re-run: that is the documented per-patch reverse-check blind spot and NOT an
upstream change. The cure is the recorded one —
`git -C irisgl/thirdparty/ogre-next checkout -- . &&
git -C irisgl/thirdparty/ogre-next clean -fd` and re-run the script.

WHY (Jahshaka lane PHOTON-M2, 2026-09-17, measured; finding F-A of the physics
read at ledger §659, and F2 of the 2026-09-17 render audit's PHOTON section).

THE UNIT CHAIN, from the lamp to the pixel.

  * `light.diffuse` in the injection's const buffer is `colour * powerScale` = D,
    and in this tree D = pi * I for the document's intensity I (IrisGL does not
    divide by pi; HlmsPbs does — kD = albedo/pi,
    `OgreHlmsPbsDatablock.cpp:82-84`).
  * The Lambertian OUTGOING RADIANCE of a voxel's surface is therefore
    L_out = rho * E / pi = rho * NdotL * D / pi, which is exactly what HlmsPbs
    computes for the DIRECT lighting of the same surface.
  * What the injection stored was `NdotL * D * rho * shadow` = pi * L_out
    (`LightInjection_piece_cs.any:162`). The intended constant for the missing
    factor is in the file, named `c_invPI` — and it was VALUED pi and never used.
  * The cone gather downstream is a weighted mean of those voxels over a
    cosine-ish set of six cones (weights summing to 1) — an estimate of E/pi —
    and HlmsPbs consumes it as `envColourD` with no division of its own
    (`200.BRDFs_piece_ps.any:305`: Rd = envColourD * albedo). So the cone-lit
    DIFFUSE was pi times brighter than the EMISSIVE and the AMBIENT sharing the
    same voxel slot, both of which are radiance already (the emissive is written
    straight through, and `VctLighting::fillConstBufferData` scales the ambient
    pair by `invFinalMultiplier` so the decode returns it unchanged).
  * The SPECULAR path carried a hard-coded `0.31831f` — 1/pi — under upstream's
    own comment "but I'm not sure why is it even needed. It's clearly
    overbrightened when it's not there". That is this pi, found by eye: it made
    the specular cone right and left the diffuse one wrong.

AND IT IS WHAT THE 8-BIT VOLUME CAN HOLD. The store is scaled by
`bakingMultiplier = pi / D_max` (`VctLighting::update`'s autoMultiplier), so with
the pi the stored value was `pi * rho * NdotL * D / D_max` — above 1, i.e.
CLIPPED, for every surface with `rho * NdotL * D / D_max > 1/pi`, which is most
lit surfaces. Clipping an RGB triple channel by channel desaturates it: a red wall
at (1.0, 0.31, 0.31) bleeds pink. Without the pi the stored value is
`rho * NdotL * D / D_max`, at most exactly 1 — the whole 8-bit range, used and
never exceeded.

THE FIX: `c_invPI` is given its name's value (0.318309886) and applied to the
direct term, and the specular path's `0.31831f` is deleted from both the composite
and patch 0048's exported escape colour (which must remove exactly what was
added, so the sky swap stays exact).

MEASURED (spikes/photon-m2):

  * THE ANALYTIC FORM FACTOR, `m2-bounceA.js` — a large floor of albedo rho_f
    under a vertical sun with the ambient off, and a wall standing on it. A point
    on the wall sees the floor over half its hemisphere, so
    L_wall / L_floor = rho_w / 2 = 0.5 exactly, with no units, no exposure and no
    light intensity in the answer. Three probes up the wall, floor probes in
    front of it:
        base        0.800  0.726  0.637   (predicted 0.500)
        this patch  0.521  0.475  0.412
    The lowest probe — the one where the half-space approximation holds — lands
    within 4 % of the analytic answer; the fall-off up the wall is the form
    factor doing what it should. (The base's 1.6x rather than pi is the 8-bit
    clip compressing the ratio: the floor's own voxels were saturated.)
  * THE SPECULAR AMBIENT, which this patch also un-darkens by pi: the scene's one
    ambient (`OgreScene::setAmbient`'s single convention) now reaches the
    specular slot as it reaches the diffuse one. Three suites measure it and were
    re-anchored with the numbers: gi.volume_edge (+2/255 on a 24/255 band at the
    volume's face, attributed by zeroing the term in staged media — the band
    returns to the GI-off value exactly), gi.chain_face (face step 1.029 ->
    1.057) and gi.rt_reflect (the no-ray control's red excess 0.0099 -> 0.0315,
    the ray arm's answer unchanged).

THE SELFTEST: this patch alone moves `--engine-selftest` from `277ba3c2…` to
`8254977e…` — 54,228 of 65,536 pixels by at most 6/255, every changed channel
DARKER. With 0076 it reads `ebe346e1…`.
